Hello!

When booting, after loading the initrd and progressing with device detectio=
n, the kernel will usually stop continuing and instead repeatedly output (w=
ith varying type and page parameters):
mptbase: ioc0: WARNING - Issuing Reset from mpt_config!!, doorbell=3D0x2400=
0000
mptbase: ioc0: Attempting Retry Config request type 0x1, page 0x1, action 0
mptbase: ioc0: WARNING - Issuing Reset from mpt_config!!, doorbell=3D0x2400=
0000
mptbase: ioc0: Initiating recovery

It will not recover from that state. It appears that if I let the kernel co=
ntinue until it reaches:
WARNING: CPU: 1 PID: 17 at /usr/src/linux-3.12.8-gentoo/mm/page_alloc.c:248=
3=20
__alloc_pages_nodemask+0x460/0x1180()
[...]
scsi target2:0:0: mptspi: ioc0: dma_alloc_coherent for parameters failed

(the SCSI devices will still not be accessible) and then hard-reset the mac=
hine, it will successfully boot on the next try.


[4.] Kernel information
[4.1.] Kernel version:
The latest version that shows the problem is 3.12.8.

[4.2.] Kernel .config file:
Please find the config for 3.12.8-gentoo attached.
The same issue appears with all vanilla kernels in the range I tested, so I=
 am confident the Gentoo patches are not causing this.


[5.] Most recent kernel version which did not have the bug:
Both problems first appeared with Linux 3.9.10 after updating from 3.8.10.
Since then I tested 3.10.8 and onward and 3.12.2 and newer and all suffer f=
rom this problem.


[6.] Output of Oops:
Please find the complete boot logs (and configs) for version 3.9.10 at foll=
owing bugreports:
https://bugzilla.kernel.org/show_bug.cgi?id=3D60566
https://bugzilla.kernel.org/show_bug.cgi?id=3D60567

The boot log for a hang situation with 3.12.8-gentoo is attached.


